Z||000012||fiero56||01-18-2001||12:41 AM||||I've never had any Fiero dreams that I remember. I had a friend once tell me that in their dream I was pi$$ed at my Fiero because I couldn't get something on it perfect, so I ended up setting it on fire, and pushing it off a cliff(???) saying something about seeing it do that(whatever was bugging me) now. <BR>Those who know of my perfectionistic(some say "engineering") attitude, know that if it could be better, it's not right and it bugs the crap out of me until it's right.||||reg||1
Z||000013||DaRkLoRD||01-18-2001||01:13 AM||||I have weird dreams all the time.. and since I've been studying psychology (an interest of mine) for several years now, I understand that most aren't caused by anything we eat, but are actually symbolic images from our subconscious as we try to process information gathered during the day. Often seemingly unrelated images can appear in the dream, because things we learned during that day have subconscious links to other memories.. you might not remember how a fiero part related to a symbolic toy shop, but somewhere there's a link.. it all depends on what the toy store symbolizes though.<BR>One thing is certain though, most people don't pay enough attention to their dreams....<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000014||FieroLisa||01-18-2001||01:17 AM||||Last year in school we had to analyze our dreams using a dream dictionary- most of it didnt make sense, one object would mean one thing, another action would mean another and they never made sense. Then again the dream I analyzed was about peanut brittle laced with hallucinogens  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Who knows...<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (Sold!)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/pffsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||DaRkLoRD||01-18-2001||02:15 AM||||I've done a bit of dream analysis, and I've found that a LOT of the symbols do mean the same thing, conveying a similar message about an issue your subconscious is trying to deal with.<P>Not every dream works out that well of course.. but if you analyze enough of them, you'll see that many do. Of course, it helps if you can remember your dreams. I've trained myself to recall multiple dreams from each night..<BR>For what it's worth, I'm more in favor of Jung's school of thinking than Freud's. and I too have had a Fiero dream.. a lucid dream actually.. but that's another story, it was so weird I should probably get a professional to analyze it.. along with some of my recurring dream symbols...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
