Z||000018||FieroLisa||01-18-2001||08:13 AM||||roy- are ya sure you're not day dreaming?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (Sold!)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/pffsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000019||fierogt88||01-18-2001||08:51 AM||||The only dream I've ever had about my fiero involved my sister-in-law... we were trying to "make-out" but couldn't really do it in the fiero. Shhh!! don't let that get back to my wife!<P>Actually, one of the current theories on dreams says that there is one part of the brain blasting random signals out when we're asleep and our conciousness tries to make sense out of the signals.  So the brain is trying to match up recent memories with these random signals, and that is why we seem to "think" about things that happened to us recently.  But the randomness can cause some seriously strange things that no one would normally think up, and can even create new "fake" memories and stuff.  The show I saw where they were talking about this they even were studying animals and relating this to human conciousness. i.e. dogs had this same random signal thing as well as monkeys, but not cattle or mice, even though they all seemed to have brain "thought" activity while sleeping.<P>At least I _hope_ it was random insanity...||||reg||6
Z||000020||mrfixit58||01-18-2001||09:02 AM||||Hey, wait a minute... those weren't super models, they were Fiero Lisa and her friends!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Nice web site Lisa!<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
