Z||000022||TheFiero64||01-18-2001||10:55 AM||||I had a dream that I went outside and there was a guy sitting in my Fiero. I ran out yelling and he said he was just looking at it. He wanted to know if it was for sale. I said no, and it will not be ether. He said sorry and got in a big box truck and started to leave. I looked back and my 86 GT was a subframe up on blocks. I said #$%@ He just stripped my car. I got in my 88 to follow him and it had the int. stripped too. It was not a good dream. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||9
Z||000023||Cheever2||01-18-2001||12:38 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by hugh:<BR><B>I also dream in color sometimes,but not very often.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Since the notion of black-and-white-only images came about when photography was invented, do you suppose all dreams <I>before</I> that were <B>always</B> in color?  I mean, if nobody had even considered the possibility of visualizing something in just black and white, how could even their subconscious minds have conceived it?<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000024||Raydar||01-18-2001||01:19 PM||||A few months ago, I had a dream that I found my 1st GT, that I bought new in 85, and traded in 88. In the dream, it was still white, but looked more like a 2nd gen MR-2 with t-tops. Was in a drive-under garage, at some old lady's condo, all covered with construction sawdust, but otherwise immaculate. Only had like 29000 miles on it. The old lady didn't want it, and was my wife ever gonna be mad when I got home with it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000025||Jaygee79||01-22-2001||05:54 PM||||I had a Fiero related dream once.  I dreamt that my car was outside and i went out to get into it and the outside looked fine but the inside (where you sit) was completely charred.  It was horrible.||||reg||1
Z||000026||StuGood||01-22-2001||11:25 PM||||Wonder why the gold ones get into dreams?  In 1994, I used to get to work in the predawn hours before anyone else, so that I could work 4-day (10 hour per day) work weeks.  The extra day off was great, but I would usually walk in from the (empty) parking lot alone, at this particular facility.  The surrounding neighborhood wasn't the best, and it was pretty dark and lonely.<P>Anyway, one time I dreamt that I was standing there in the dark parking lot, looking over towards the building, and in the shadows I saw my gold 1986 SE sitting there on blocks, near the front of the building.  The car was okay, but the wheels and tires were gone.  I think at first I felt a little fear, but for some reason, in a moment it didn't bother me too much; I just thought, "Well, I guess I'll have to find some more wheels and tires." <P>Then I started waking up.  I realized that I was at home in bed.  At first, I wanted to go out and look at my car (in the garage) and see if everything was okay.  But as I woke up more, I started thinking it was probably okay, and even if anything had happened to the car, it was already done.  Worrying about it now wasn't going to change it, and it's just a car anyhow.  I went back to sleep, and if I remember, slept very soundly - it felt good.         <P>Well, that's my only Fiero dream, in excruciating detail.  Interpretations? ||||reg||5
Z||000027||1FST2M6||01-23-2001||08:25 AM||||LMAO!!! Jeff.. you've got some ISSUES! that need to be delt with BEFORE you come down here!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> hehehehe anyone got a hotwheels GT? if so i'll paint it orange and carry it in my pocket everyday!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   thats not as bad as having a picture of your car in your wallet is it?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000028||COUNTIBLIS||01-23-2001||08:58 AM||||I dream about what i think about for a split second during the day.  then my mind makes a damn story out of it.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000029||Tigger||01-23-2001||09:23 AM||||I've had the accident dream before, can't remember exactly, but someone ran into my Fiero pretty good.  I woke up with the idea I'd have to start looking for a donar car to put things back together, a moment later I realized it was just a dream.  Phew!<P>Another was almost in a Mad Max kind of setting, but inside a dark city.  I lived above a small abandoned greasy repair shop, and kept my Fiero parked in the service bay.  For some reason the shop was like one of the best places to be in at the time because car parts and tools were in short order.  It was funny because everything in the shop was dark and dingy except for my Fiero.  I had retrofitted it with most of the high tech stuff that was available at the time.  The rest is too sketchy to explain, but it was sweet.  Took me a minute to regain my marbles and figure out it was just a dream.  It seemed so real.  Those are the best.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Ta Ta For Now!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue3.gif"> ||||reg||1
